!! Findings

''The brief’s “CRDT-only control plane” description is true of the current layout, but it hides a mismatch:'' `bags/daemon` is both the daemon wiki’s canon bag and the name used for vessel control records. The code explicitly treats every title under that URI as control-plane data and excludes it from disk projection, even when the record sits in another layer. [[lar-uris.ts:345–352|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-mesh/src/lar-uris.ts:345]] [[disk-projector.ts:1520–1528|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-node/src/disk-projector.ts:1520]]

!!! 1. Writers and data kinds

Kinds: ''S'' secret or opaque bytes that may contain secrets; ''E'' signed public events/proofs; ''R'' ordinary machine records. A record’s envelope can be R while its payload is unsafe to expose.

| Title family | Production writer(s) | Kind and notes |h
| `summons`, `outcomes`, `effects` | `verb-tiddler.ts`, `verb-vm.ts`, dispatcher/VM paths | ''R'' envelopes/results; outcomes may embed arbitrary handler results, so their payload is not proven secret-free. `effects` is also excluded by the projector’s separate effect-record filter. [[verb-tiddler.ts:59–65|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-mesh/src/verb-tiddler.ts:59]] [[verb-vm.ts:23–27|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-tw5/src/verb-vm.ts:23]] |
| `receipts` | UDS channel via `buildReceiptFact` | ''R'' request/state/digest metadata; inputs are represented by digests, not copied argument bodies. [[verb-tiddler.ts:110–121,219–239|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-mesh/src/verb-tiddler.ts:110]] |
| `mailbox` | `vessel-mailbox.ts` | ''R'', request/action/args; arbitrary args mean payload sensitivity is caller-dependent. |
| `delegate`, `face-row` | `daemon-vm-core.ts` | ''R'' invocation records that include args; likewise not safe to project without payload controls. [[daemon-vm-core.ts:672–682,828–833|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-tw5/src/daemon-vm-core.ts:672]] |
| `cap/<face>/<hash>` | `DaemonEventStore.put` | ''S (conservative)'': stores base64-encoded raw Keyhive event bytes and replays them. The schema does not establish that every variant is secret-free. [[daemon-event-store.ts:58–61,83–110|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-keyhive/src/daemon-event-store.ts:58]] |
| `lease-epoch`, `ledger/proof`, `ledger/ward` | lease frontier; proof/supervision and ward paths | ''E/R'': signed lease/proof or audit facts and their metadata. Keep as public machine records only if their actual fields remain public. [[epoch-lease.ts:9–16|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-mesh/src/epoch-lease.ts:9]] [[wiki-sense-supervision.ts:89–107|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-tw5/src/wiki-sense-supervision.ts:89]] |
| `pin/<bag-url>`, `ledger/residency/<event>` | bag-residency/effect-record paths | ''R'' pin and residency records; effect records are separately filtered from projection. [[bag-residency.ts:509–517|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-mesh/src/bag-residency.ts:509]] [[effect-record.ts:68–80|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-mesh/src/effect-record.ts:68]] |
| `hearth/{sync-url,gate-key,gate-pin,doc-url,island-kind,island-scope,daemon-url}`, `sentinel/mesh-cabal/doc-id`, `active-wiki` | `hearth-dial-pin.ts`, `lar-uris.ts`, `active-wiki.ts` and their callers | ''R/E'' metadata, URLs, IDs and a public gate key/pin; the cited title definitions do not show private key bytes. [[lar-uris.ts:581–591|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-mesh/src/lar-uris.ts:581]] [[active-wiki.ts:8–42|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-tw5/src/active-wiki.ts:8]] |
| `flows/<name>` | flow URI/flow paths | ''R'' executable flow definition; inspect its cap stack as policy/code, not as a key store. [[lar-uris.ts:386–390|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-mesh/src/lar-uris.ts:386]] |
| `task/<cid>`, `receipt/<task-cid>` | URI builders only | ''No production writer found'' in the current task/receipt ontology code; it says the live path has not migrated yet. [[verb-tiddler.ts:69–87|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-mesh/src/verb-tiddler.ts:69]] |
| `draft-bindings`, `working-bindings` | No `bags/daemon` writer found | Binding records are checked/lifted by binding code, but the namespace is persona-scoped; do not relocate them on the basis of this title-family list. |

''Key-shaped content check:'' the definite opaque key-material risk is `cap`, whose stored value is arbitrary serialized event bytes. The other listed schemas show public keys/IDs or ordinary records, but `outcomes`, `mailbox`, `delegate`, and `face-row` carry extensible payloads. Treat them as non-projectable until payload policy is enforced; title family alone does not prove safety.

!!! 2. Readers and name assumptions

A production source scan for `DAEMON_BAG_ID`, `bags/daemon`, `isControlPlaneUri`, and `kahuaFaceFolder` found direct assumptions across these modules:

* ''URI ownership/filtering and composition:'' `lararium-mesh/{lar-uris,wiki-recipe,register-bags,catalog-view,open-vessel-core,flow,epoch-lease,bag-residency,cabal-realm,social-seed}.ts`.
* ''Verb, request, and result paths:'' `lararium-mesh/verb-tiddler.ts`; `lararium-tw5/{verb-vm,verb-dispatcher,verb-summons,daemon-vm-core,active-wiki,wiki-mint-handlers,worker-data-verbs,verb-local-dispatch,modules/reaction-router,wiki-sense-supervision}.ts`; `lararium-node/{uds-channel,vessel-mailbox}.ts`.
* ''Keyhive, bindings, and replay:'' `lararium-keyhive/{daemon-event-store,event-store,ceremony-core,operator-daemon-behavior,lease-frontier,resolve-binding,anon-lift,bag-doc-ledger}.ts`.
* ''Node boot, federation, and disk rules:'' `lararium-node/{bag-paths,disk-projector,hearth-dial-pin,boot-face-planes,open-node-vessel,nexus-client-dial}.ts` and `lararium-node/commands/{init,device-admit,cabal-join,persona-lease}.ts`; also `lararium-browser/open-browser-vessel.ts`, `lares-cli/commands/watch.ts`.

These readers fall into four important groups: event replay and verb processing; bootstrap/admission and sync audience (including `DAEMON_BAG_ID` as the default audience); catalog/binding lookup; and projection/lift filtering. `isControlPlaneUri` resolves title paths before testing the daemon prefix, and `kahua-door` rejects those titles from lifts. [[lar-uris.ts:349–352|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-mesh/src/lar-uris.ts:349]] [[kahua-door.ts:143–146|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-node/src/kahua-door.ts:143]]

''Riskiest reader to move first:'' `isControlPlaneUri` and its consumers. It currently makes the entire `bags/daemon/**` title space non-projectable and non-liftable, including outcomes regardless of which composite layer contains them. Renaming only a folder would leave that policy in force.

!!! 3. The three “kahua” meanings

# ''Lift-only bag/stage:'' `bags/kahua`, mounted read-only; a normal edit copies up to the working layer, while a signed lift lands in the stage. [[wiki-recipe.ts:74–76,381–389|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-mesh/src/wiki-recipe.ts:74]]
# ''Working mirror directory:'' currently `wikis/kahua-<F>`. Its bag/layer identity is still `wikis/daemon/working`; only the projection folder is face-tagged. The stage bag separately projects to `bags/kahua-<F>`. With no face, neither private mirror is listed. [[bag-paths.ts:148–179,186–209|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-node/src/bag-paths.ts:148]]
# ''Memory title namespace:'' a title such as `lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/<row-key>` does ''not'' by itself identify the backing bag. `resolveTopmost`/layer ownership does.

''The stage location is not consistently documented.'' The current layer ruling says rows become stage rows at the daemon wiki’s ''working seam'' and readers use working plus canon, not drafts; the working projection is currently `wikis/kahua-<F>`. [[stable-founding-road.mem:382|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:382]] But the earlier L19 description says “kahua working top” and “never the daemon wiki,” then has L21 lift verified batches. [[kahua-memory-stage.mem:257–259|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/kahua-memory-stage.mem:257]] The best reading is that ''stage/proposal rows are working-layer content; lifted canon is in `bags/kahua`'', but those documents conflict on which wiki owns that working layer. I found no production TypeScript writer for the memory rows to settle the conflict. Lift requires the face’s lōkahi capability and an operator root grant; the device atom may propose, but cannot substitute for the grant. [[kahua-door.ts:13–18,143–180|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-node/src/kahua-door.ts:13]]

!!! 4. Face binding and canon

A worn face supplies `faceRelation`; `kahuaFaceFolder` validates it and names the private projection folder. No-face compositions omit both the daemon working and kahua-stage mirrors. The daemon bag identity itself remains the vessel’s static `bags/daemon`. [[bag-paths.ts:148–170,186–209|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-node/src/bag-paths.ts:148]] [[open-node-vessel.ts:3265–3278|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-node/src/open-node-vessel.ts:3265]]

Under the operator’s wiki pattern, a face-bound daemon wiki’s promoted canon would naturally be `bags/daemon-<F>`, with its working mirror at `wikis/daemon-<F>`. ''That is an inference from the pattern'', not the current URI scheme: today the daemon wiki’s own canon is `bags/daemon`, and its working slot is `wikis/daemon/working`. [[wiki-recipe.ts:15–17,83–89|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-mesh/src/wiki-recipe.ts:15]]

Per-vessel records must not silently become face-scoped: the hearth URL, MeshCabal document ID, leases, and vessel control/verb records serve the vessel, which wears no face. The founding law says one Lararium per human and that a session wears a face while the vessel wears none. [[stable-founding-road.mem:157–159|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:157]] It also calls for a floor/face split: vessel floor core versus each face’s daemon wiki content. [[stable-founding-road.mem:338–339|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:338]]

!!! 5. Lean and migration surface

''Inference / proposed lean:'' create a persisted, vessel-scoped `control` layer for R and verified-public E records, with one alpha projection toggle. Keep opaque `cap` bytes and any secret-bearing seals/checkpoints in a never-projected secret home. Restore `bags/daemon[-F]` to the wiki’s promoted canon, use `wikis/daemon-<F>` for its working projection, and reserve `bags/kahua` for the lift-governed stage. Keep vessel-scoped control records distinct from a face-bound wiki’s canon.

The direct production reference inventory above is the code surface a rename/move must audit, not merely rename: URI/type and recipe definitions; registration and catalogs; projection; boot, admission, and sync audience; verb, mailbox, and result readers/writers; event replay and bindings; CLI and browser readers. In particular, review `lar-uris.ts`, `wiki-recipe.ts`, `register-bags.ts`, `bag-paths.ts`, `disk-projector.ts`, `daemon-vm-core.ts`, `open-node-vessel.ts`, `open-browser-vessel.ts`, `daemon-event-store.ts`, `kahua-door.ts`, and generated TW5 bundle `plugin-tiddler.generated.ts`. The busiest/riskiest assumptions are the global prefix filter, composite’s daemon bag mounting, and `DAEMON_BAG_ID` as sync audience.

This move would breach canon law if it created a Lararium/state mount per face or moved vessel-wide control under one face’s authority. Keeping the one vessel and splitting only face-specific wiki content is compatible with the cited law. It must also preserve recipe law: working is the normal write layer; canon changes only by promotion move; kahua accepts only signed lift acts. [[wiki-recipe.ts:15–17,351–356|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/packages/lararium-mesh/src/wiki-recipe.ts:15]] [[stable-founding-road.mem:158–159|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road.mem:158]]

//Read-only hand-back; no files changed.//

